WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:13.530
<i>I'm about to be married to the one I love.</i>

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.120
I was searching for you long before we met.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.500
<i>Huh? Two grooms?</i>

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.760
<i>Someya-kun? Shibasaki-kun?</i>

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.980
I love you.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:33.840
I love you.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:34.910
<i>Huh?</i>

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.340
Huh?!

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.040
Will you...

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:38.910
Will you...

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.870
...marry me?

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.490
<i>Huh?</i>

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.700
<i>Wait... Wait a second!</i>

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.280
<i>Wait—</i>

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.960
I-It was a dream...

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.510
Why did I dream that?!

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.470
<i>I'm charmed by how you go all-out</i>

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.970
<i>I'm charmed by your supportive smile</i>

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.350
<i>"I must kiss you," says your Romeo</i>

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.310
<i>Glad that you exist and that he met you</i>

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.540
<b>Heroines Run the Show</b>

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:38.950
<i>I need more love, want to see you again soon</i>

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.040
<i>Lock eyes with you and tell you</i>

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.960
<i>My sincerest "Thank you for everything"</i>

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.210
<i>Will you love me—not 
as a fan, but for real?</i>

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.250
<i>"Pick me"</i>

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.970
<i>"No, pick me"</i>

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.850
<i>Choose which kiss you want</i>

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.030
<i>And let your Romeo bind you</i>

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.470
<i>I'm charmed by how you go all-out</i>

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:15.030
<i>I'm charmed watching you sing with me</i>

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.340
<i>I'm even charmed by your tears</i>

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.740
<i>I'm charmed by your supportive smile</i>

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.370
<i>Thank you for coming to meet me</i>

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.660
<i>Thank you for calling my name</i>

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.210
<i>"I must kiss you," says your Romeo</i>

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:39.400
<i>Glad that you exist and that he met you</i>

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.790
You seem happy.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.320
Does it show? Yes, offers for
 LIP×LIP are pouring in!

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.810
It must be the "Nonfantasy" 
music video effect.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.410
It must be hard work when 
things get this busy.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.990
I'm more than happy to be busy!

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:09.870
It's a manager's pleasure to 
see her artists make it big.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.230
Hello, you two!

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.560
Hello.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.420
Hello, ma'am.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.300
Hey.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.390
<i>T-Too close!</i>

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.330
Why are you avoiding eye contact?

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.050
Got something you want to say to us?

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.310
N-No...

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.150
Cutlet sandwich.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.400
Tuna mayo rice ball.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:38.700
Huh?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.730
Go <i>buy</i> them!

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.950
And no convenience store crap. 
Go to the bakery at the station.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:44.980
You have five minutes.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.690
Get the rice ball at the 
convenience store. Move it!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.110
Dash!

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.830
<i>Argh! These two suck.</i>

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.550
<i>They're so mean!</i>

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.370
<i>That dream means nothin'. 
It was temporary insanity!</i>

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.090
<i>Those two are...</i>

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.410
...the last ones I'd marry!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.290
Any comments on the design or anything?

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.330
I think it's good!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.890
It's better than I imagined.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.430
The rosettes were a great idea.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.400
Rosettes?

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:22.580
They're free gifts for the 
fans at our next event.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.160
Aizo and Yujiro thought of them.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.660
Apparently they were inspired by the 
first-place medals at athletic meets!

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:34.420
The sentiment is, "Thanks for 
supporting us. You're number one."

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.580
Fans will be thrilled with them!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:42.010
I was so happy to get a first-place medal.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:44.630
So, is this...

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.660
No way. Don't be ridiculous.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.270
Just hand over my rice ball.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.440
I saw your new music video! It was so moving!

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.960
It's a great song!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.240
Thank you.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.740
I'm glad to hear it.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.660
<i>Man... They're gettin' even more 
attention than usual today.</i>

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.860
Idols are amazing. They've got a harem!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:18.520
Marrying those two in a church is the 
kind of video girls freak out over.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.900
It's trending, so bandwagon fans 
are hyped right now, that's all.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:27.350
You sure know a lot. Are you 
interested in them too, Chizuru?

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.640
I just happened to see it on TV, that's all.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.290
<i>Are they gonna be okay?</i>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.460
Hey, Aizo, what kind of girl is your type?

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.410
Are you dating anyone?

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.810
Do you want to get married someday?

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.410
Aizo, are you okay?

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.540
What's wrong?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.390
<i>Uh-oh, he's reached his limit!</i>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:55.650
Shibasaki-kun must be <i>really</i> workin' hard! 
He seemed <i>really</i> sleepy all morning!

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.290
Huh? You mean he fell asleep?

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.960
That suddenly?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.760
We worked late last night.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:07.090
He sometimes passes out like this 
if he doesn't get enough sleep.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.340
Oh, wow.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.330
Maybe he should get some 
sleep in the nurse's office?

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.640
I can escort him.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.420
Me, too!

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.420
Me, too!

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.400
Me, too!

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.400
Me, too!

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.020
That won't do.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:19.020
I'm Aizo's escort.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.240
Oh, of course!

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.070
You're friends, after all.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:23.860
Wake up.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.220
Let's go.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.400
Okay...

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:36.190
Um, I'll go tell the teacher what happened.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.500
See you later!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.730
Your trauma is getting awkward.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:44.590
Trauma?

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.220
Hey, keep your mouth shut.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.730
Did something happen?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.300
It's nothing.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.550
It's not nothing! You collapsed.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.310
It's none of your business!

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.930
I'm your manager, you know!

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.690
Yeah, <i>in training</i>!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:08.070
<b>Guidance Office</b>

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.070
Is it okay for us to be in here?

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.730
Yep. I've got Akechi-sensei's permission

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:14.050
to use this room whenever we need it.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:21.810
Third period is about to start. 
What do you want to do?

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.860
We'll rest here. I'll stay with him.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.330
Okay. I'll tell the teacher.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:39.630
You're an idol who's uncomfortable with girls...

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.390
You really need to get used to them.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.400
It's not like I don't want to change.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.780
<b>School Store</b>

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.670
Yes! I scored a bun!

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.760
<i>Maybe he'd eat a sandwich?</i>

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.380
<i>What would a boy like?</i>

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:11.240
Cutlet sandwich! One cutlet sandwich, please!

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.530
Cutlet sandwich!

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.430
Hello, ma'am! Can I get a cutlet sandwich?

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:19.680
Sure thing.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.190
Here you go.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.960
Thank you very much.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.070
You're welcome, Suzumi Hiyori-san
 from class 1-4.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.610
Huh? Why d'ya know my name?

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:39.540
You're Aizo's girlfriend, right?

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:40.620
Gir—

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:44.210
N-N-N-No, I'm not!

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.600
Oh, you're not?

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:50.400
I just assumed from the friendly 
bickering that you were.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.020
Who are you, anyway?

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:56.640
I'm Shibasaki Ken, second-year.
 Nice to meet you.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.600
I'm Aizo's big brother!

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.320
What?! Big brother?!

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.480
Oh...

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.930
You do look alike. 
You've got the same face!

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:09.220
Right?

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:14.490
Huh, come to think of it, Aizo told 
me to pretend I didn't know him.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:17.130
Keep this a secret, okay, Hiyori-chan?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:21.010
You seem fine around girls.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.760
Yeah, why?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:28.890
Shibasaki-kun—I mean, Aizo-kun—
seems uncomfortable with girls.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:32.670
Oh, right. That's because of me and my mom.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.510
Mom's got a different man every five minutes,

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.130
and I went through a playboy phase.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.210
He's a strait-laced guy, 
so that stuff isn't okay with him.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.470
Oh, thank goodness.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:55.250
They called it "trauma," so I thought 
something really bad happened to him.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.900
I'm glad it didn't.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:01.150
There are so many nice girls out there, too.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:04.330
How can we help him be comfortable?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.540
You're a nice girl, Hiyori-chan.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.290
Huh?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.570
Take care of my brother!

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:15.250
What's that s'posed to mean?

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:20.180
It's me! I'm comin' in!

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:25.310
You brought lunch, Someya-kun? 
What about Shibasaki-kun?

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.880
He said he planned to buy something.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.710
I bought a cutlet sandwich. Do you want it?

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:35.440
I'm not really hungry.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:41.160
You know, I'm not comfortable with squid.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.240
What?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.530
Squid?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:49.320
I'm a fisherman's daughter, 
and my town is famous for squid,

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.790
so I want to say that I love squid.

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:57.490
But no matter how much I try, I just 
really hate the squooshy texture...

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.410
I understand how you feel, 
bein' uncomfortable around girls.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:06.050
We can't help what makes 
us uncomfortable, right?

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:10.330
Huh? Did I say something funny?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:14.570
You bet that's funny. You think girls 
and squid belong in the same category?

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:17.690
Well, the fact that we don't 
like them is the same!

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:23.320
From now on, I'm gonna remember squid 
whenever I'm surrounded by girls.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.550
Is that all you're having for lunch?

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:32.020
Yep! The buns in the school store 
are a great deal for their size.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.460
And tasty, too!

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.380
That's not what I mean.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:39.770
Shouldn't you be thinking about 
nutrient balance, since you do sports?

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.600
Have some if you want.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:45.990
Whoa, that's so fancy!

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:49.000
Is it a custom lunch? 
Like from a nice restaurant?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.480
It's my mom's cooking.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.310
Oh, wow, your mom is amazin'!

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.190
She loves you a lot, huh?

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.900
She makes lunch for my father 
and brother. I'm an afterthought.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.240
Oho, you're embarrassed.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:02.240
I am not!

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.870
This omelet is nice and sweet!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.310
Hey, I was saving that for last!

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:13.580
So you're the type to eat 
his favorite thing last?

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.410
I mean, doesn't everyone?!

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.730
No, not everyone.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:18.130
What's your deal?

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.770
It's Uchida-san.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.380
Hello?

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.700
<i>Yujiro, don't leave the 
school until I get there.</i>

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.870
What? Why not?

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.020
This would be why.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:46.870
<b>The Shame of a Famous Kabuki Family?
Someya Tamagoro's Eldest Son Is a Pop Idol!</b>

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:41.780
"The Shame of a Famous Kabuki Family?"

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:46.870
"Someya Tamagoro's Eldest Son Is a Pop Idol!"

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.220
Huh?!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.460
This has really caused a stir.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:05.800
It just proves how much 
attention LIP×LIP is getting.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.890
If they weren't popular, the media
 wouldn't write about this.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:14.420
True... But this feels a little malicious.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.310
<b>Top News
The Shame of a Famous Kabuki Family?
Someya Tamagoro's Eldest Son Is a Pop Idol!</b>

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:17.460
It's obviously lies!

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.290
All that stuff about "disowning" 
and "parent-child strife" is wrong.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:24.950
No mom would make such a love-filled 
lunch for a child she hates!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.910
I'm gonna tell the reporters to go home!

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.700
Stay out of this.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:35.340
A lecture from a manager-in-training 
won't make the media back down.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.420
But...

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:43.480
If I know you, you saw this coming.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.630
You anticipated that you couldn't 
hide your family forever.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.510
Go fight them head-on.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:56.070
I don't need you to tell me that.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.170
Someya-san!

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.310
Someya Yujiro-san!

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:01.770
Someya-san!

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.530
Someya-san, comment please!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:02.930
Someya-san!

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.090
Good evening, everyone.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:07.460
Someya Yujiro-san,

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:12.360
why did you keep quiet about being 
the heir to a famous kabuki family?

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:16.420
I'm sure if I'd openly claimed my family 
name, it would've gotten me attention.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:20.670
But I wanted to build my idol 
career on my own merits.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.390
Why would a Someya choose to be a pop idol?

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:27.380
Kabuki actor Someya Tamagoro has been 
called a living national treasure.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.920
Didn't you train under him?

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:35.010
As a child, I wanted to be a kabuki actor, 
and I took lessons from my father.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.540
But I abandoned that dream.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:38.810
Why is that?

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:42.020
Because of my younger brother, Koichiro.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:46.530
Koichiro is incredibly talented, he's charismatic,

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.030
and he's the hardest worker I know.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.280
He's the best heir to the Someya tradition.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.230
Did Tamagoro-san say that?

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:57.650
What did your father think 
of you becoming a pop idol?

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:00.670
Hi, everyone!

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.920
I'm Aizo, the other half of LIP×LIP!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:09.220
Aizo-san, did you know that your 
partner was the Someya family heir?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.490
Of course!

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:14.570
Man, was I bowled over 
when I went to his house.

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:16.620
Their gate is huge!

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:20.290
And did you know he does his own makeup?

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:23.440
I was like, "He's a dude, so why
 is he so good at makeup?"

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.120
I imagined some reasons,

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:29.820
and I was relieved to learn 
it was the kabuki thing.

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:35.080
But any reason would 
be fine. Yujiro is Yujiro.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:42.430
Frankly, I'm glad he didn't 
go the kabuki route!

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:45.980
I mean, we'd be lonely 
without each other. Right?

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.330
I wouldn't be lonely.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.900
Wait, you don't return my feelings?!

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.580
Well... I guess it was encouraging

00:15:55.940 --> 00:16:00.890
to have a partner who's 
chasing the same dream as me.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:06.180
Both of us are serious 
about our idol careers.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:08.890
Be sure to check out Yujiro's next moves!

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.820
You mean <i>our</i> next moves.

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:11.990
Good point.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:17.490
<i>They're constantly fightin', but at 
times like these, they help each other.</i>

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:20.370
<i>It's so movin'!</i>

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:24.420
I'll be fielding any further questions.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.510
Welcome back! Would you 
like your coffee and cocoa?

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:34.890
Sure.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:35.470
Yeah.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.510
I'm on it!

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:41.060
What's got her so enthusiastic?

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.050
Who knows?

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:51.570
<i>What else can a manager-in-training do?</i>

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:55.630
<i>I wish I could be more useful...</i>

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:02.040
<b><i>Free Concert & Autograph Session</i></b>

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:06.420
This is our first performance after 
the article. Don't you half-ass it.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.900
Don't <i>you</i> get carried away 
and make it a one-man show.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:20.460
It's still early, but there's a crowd already!

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:24.660
Yes, they gained even more 
fans after the media tizzy.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:32.380
Oh, it's Chutan-san again!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.630
Thank you for your support.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:36.530
I look forward
 to the concert!
 -Chutan

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:40.240
What? You left the rosettes 
back at the office?!

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.410
I'm so sorry!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.930
We all forget things sometimes.

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.940
At least we never announced a 
free gift, so there's no probl—

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.670
I'll go get them!

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:52.250
That's impossible.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.070
There's no time for you to—

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:54.380
We don't know until we try!

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:00.570
Here, the office key and taxi fare.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:02.930
I'll be back!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.640
Remember to get a receipt!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.160
I will!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.560
Thanks for waiting, everyone!

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:13.800
We are...

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.280
...LIP×LIP!

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:23.280
<i>We'll be in love for decades, for centuries</i>

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:29.040
<i>We'll always be drawn to 
each other, like magic</i>

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.670
Taxi!

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:43.850
<i>You know what? Tonight in my dreams</i>

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:49.130
<i>You've fallen in love with me</i>

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.250
There! There they are!

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:54.250
<i>Listen, in the picture book of our future</i>

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:55.570
I'm cutting it close, but I should make it!

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:59.540
<i>You find love with me</i>

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.800
A traffic jam?!

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>If the mischievous god of love</i>

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.880
Maybe there was an accident.

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.370
I don't think we'll be moving for a while.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:09.590
<i>Has hurt you and made you cry</i>

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:07.570
Excuse me, I'll get off here!

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:09.850
What? But we're nowhere near the venue.

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:15.410
<i>I'll become a devil to fight him</i>

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:10.790
I'll be okay.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:13.290
Oh... Receipt, please!

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:20.600
<i>We'll be in love for decades, for centuries</i>

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:25.710
<i>We'll always be drawn to 
each other, like magic</i>

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:30.980
<i>I was searching for you long before we met</i>

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:36.190
<i>Even if we're ripped apart, 
love will bind us together</i>

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:40.980
<i>My first love will last 
for decades, for centuries</i>

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:46.520
<i>And your story will overlap with mine</i>

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.100
I <i>will</i> make it!

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:53.080
Is she back?

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.220
Autograph Session Here

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:00.220
This way to the autograph session!

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:04.970
Autograph Session Here

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:02.810
Please wait in line!

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.970
We'll let you in shortly!

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:09.320
We can't make them wait any longer. Let's go.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:13.580
Just a minute!

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:24.740
You're covered in sweat!

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.480
Wait, don't tell me you ran here?!

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.220
There was a traffic jam.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:33.580
Go! Hurry!

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:35.580
Got it.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.120
Hiyoko, are you okay?

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:44.220
Hiyoko?!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.670
Thank you for all of your support.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:54.730
These are presents from us. Please take them.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.770
I love it!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.460
I'll treasure this!

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.650
<i>The fans all like them.</i>

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.410
Hey.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:13.720
You can have this.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:15.470
We had extra.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:18.580
Thank you!

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:20.360
Good work.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:21.590
Good work today.

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.470
Good work to you, too!

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:33.520
What's wrong?

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:37.050
Nothing's wrong.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:38.810
Okay, then...

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:46.590
Ow!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>What I Can Do</b>

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:32.980
Next time, on episode 5 of 
<i>Heroines Run the Show</i>...

00:23:32.980 --> 00:23:34.580
"Idols Are Amazin'!"

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Episode 5
Idols Are Amazin'!</b>
